@startuml
!theme toy
title One interactive frame: main thread, render lane, GPU

participant "Main thread\nApplication / ApplicationEditor" as main #6CB4EE
participant "Render lane\nRenderLane" as lane #77DD77
participant "GPU + Renderer\nqueue · fence · swapchain" as gpu #FFB347

main -> main : admitClientFrame_\npacer deadline + free frame credit
main -> main : update(dt)\ninput · camera · makeFramePacket
main -> main : stage grid/triangle payloads\nupdate ImGui frontend
main -> main : render()\nconsume packet · detach UI

main -> lane : submitFrame(RenderFrameRequest)\ndrop_if_full
note right of main
  Full transport = dropped frame.
  Edits stay dirty and are re-staged;
  no edit acknowledgement.
end note

lane -> lane : runLane_ select() wake\nhandleFrameEvent_
lane -> lane : executeRenderWork_\nvalidate surface · apply staging\nprepare uploads · update passes
lane -> gpu : renderAndPresent\nacquire image
lane -> gpu : encode scene + UI passes\nfence-wait hook per draw
lane -> gpu : submit command buffer\nsignal fence value V
lane -> gpu : present()
gpu --> lane : fence V observed complete\n(async, on lane sweep)
lane -> lane : retireCompletedFrames\nrelease renderer credit
lane -> main : post RenderFrameResult\nV · presented · staging · observations
main -> main : pumpRenderCompletions_\nonLaneFrameConsumed_
main -> main : ack edits · mirror generation\nrelease reservation when frontier >= V

note over main, lane
  CPU staging application and edit acknowledgement
  are not GPU completion. Only fence V is.
end note
@enduml
